# .vibe-shieldignore — gitignore syntax.
#
# vibe-shield scans its own repository in CI (`npm run verify`). The detector
# catalogue is the one place that *must* contain literally vulnerable code and
# the exact credential shapes the rules match on, so it is excluded here rather
# than weakened. This is the same approach gitleaks and semgrep take for their
# own rule packs; every exclusion below is deliberate and reviewed.

# The detector catalogue: deliberately vulnerable examples + the literal tokens
# the rules match on (regex vocabulary, vendor key formats, file-shape probes).
src/scanner/rules/
src/scanner/lexicon.ts
src/secrets/patterns.ts
src/mcp-guard/skill-auditor.ts

# Fixtures are intentionally broken applications used by the test suite.
tests/fixtures/

# Build output and dependency trees (also pruned by the engine).
dist/
node_modules/
coverage/
